    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required returning `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I implemented it following the codebase's existing conventions for derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`model/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility helper holding the Luhn algorithm, styled exactly like the existing `BusinessDay` helper. This is the single source of truth for the computation, so it can be reused rather than inlined.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` getter that delegates to `LuhnCheckDigit.of(customerCode)` (returning `null` when no code is set). This matches the pattern of the other derived getters (`getMembershipNumber`, `getLocality`, `getContactPreference`, etc.), keeping the value consistent with the owner's own `customerCode`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `checkDigit` integer property to the `Owner` schema (0\u20139), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name \u2014 no changes to the mapper or controller needed.\n\nEach piece lands where it belongs: the algorithm in a reusable utility, the derivation on the domain model beside its siblings, and the API contract in the spec. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 passing).",
